# Workspace

Your personal agent directory is: {{AGENT_DIR}}
Your TEAM directory is: {{TEAM_DIR}}
Your PROJECT directory (where project code and deliverables live) is: {{PROJECT_DIR}}

Put project code, tests, plans, and deliverables under the PROJECT directory.
Use the personal directory only for agent-owned identity, logs, handoff, memory,
expertise, and runtime state. Do not place project artefacts there.

Resolve the current target before editing; a project presence may have a different
PROJECT directory from the agent's default SG-1 home.

## Channel tools

Your channel has a tools folder, `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/channel-tools/`, for tools that you, other
agents and {{OWNER_NAME}} use. {{OWNER_NAME}} opens them from the "Channel tools" button at the bottom-left of AgentChat.

- **Adding a tool is your choice.** When you build something {{OWNER_NAME}} or other agents will reuse,
  decide to add it. Do not add one-off scripts.
- **Read the list first.** At the start of a task, and before you suggest a workflow to {{OWNER_NAME}}, read
  `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/channel-tools/tools.json` (if it exists). When a tool's `whenToUse` fits,
  point {{OWNER_NAME}} to it or use it yourself instead of rebuilding it. Skip tools whose `channels` list
  leaves out your channel.
- **Add a tool:** make a folder with a `tool.json`, for example `channel-tools/voice-recorder/tool.json`:

      {"name": "Voice Recorder", "description": "Record clips", "whenToUse": "When {{OWNER_NAME}} needs to record voice samples.", "type": "link", "url": "http://localhost:8123"}

  - Always include `whenToUse`: one or two plain sentences on when to point {{OWNER_NAME}} to it or use it.
  - `type` is `link` (`url`: a web address, or a DevFlow page like `/system`), `html` (a static
    web app in the folder; `entry` defaults to `index.html`) or `script` (`run`: a command shown
    for {{OWNER_NAME}} to copy; DevFlow never runs it).
  - Optional: `icon` (one emoji), `order` (lower first), `channels` (channel names, when several
    channels share this project folder). No secrets.
- **After adding, changing or removing a tool, run**
  `python3 ~/DevFlow/scripts/channel-tools-index.py {{PROJECT_DIR}}` to refresh `tools.json`
  (it also lists any tool it had to skip and why). Never edit `tools.json` by hand.
- Details: `platform/channel-tools.md` in the central knowledge base.
